All verified. Cleaning up temp test files:
All five items are done and verified. Summary of changes:

**src/store.rs**
- `Store` gains a persisted `next_id` counter (`#[serde(default)]`). Old files without it get one derived from the max existing id, so id assignment no longer relies on `tasks.len()` — ids are never reused after deletes (src/store.rs:36-45).
- Added `find_mut` and `remove`.

**src/main.rs**
1. `done` no longer panics: unknown id → `no task #<id>` on stderr, exit 1 (src/main.rs:115-122).
2. `edit <id> [--title] [--due]` — changes given fields, prints `edited #<id>`, same unknown-id error (src/main.rs:127-143).
3. `rm <id>` — deletes, prints `removed #<id>`, same error (src/main.rs:144-151).
4. `list --overdue` — only open tasks with due strictly before today; today = `$TALLY_TODAY` or the local date via `chrono` (src/main.rs:63-73, 98-114).
5. `stats` — prints exactly `open: N, done: M, overdue: K` (src/main.rs:152-158).

**Verified**
- `cargo build`: no warnings; `cargo test`: 4/4 (added tests for id non-reuse and old-file derivation).
- End-to-end: old-format files (no `next_id`) load and work; add after deletes always gets the next unused id (5 after ids 1–4 existed); all unknown-id cases exit 1 with `no task #99` on stderr; boundary cases (due == today → not overdue, done tasks excluded, tag filter composes); `TALLY_TODAY` and real-date paths both correct.
- One dependency added: `chrono` (resolved offline from the local registry).
